# Tether language and product spec

This file is the repo host (`root.tether`). It describes tether itself.

@ref src/extract/types.ts#Tether

doc {

# Invariants

- Git is required. Extraction and facts are functions of the tree plus history. There is no second ledger.
- Location is the bind. A comment on a declaration binds to that declaration. A sidecar binds to the sibling file or directory. `root.tether` binds to the repository.
- No bind table. Optional `@ref` and `@symbol` are extra named targets, never the host.
- Facts only. The tool emits only what git + extract + AST can recompute. No severity, no age, no "meaningful change," no attest command.
- No independent doctrine files. Tracked `*.md` and `*.txt` are `rogue_document` unless allowlisted, honorary, empty or whitespace-only, or conventional fixture inputs.
- The full wiki is derived and never committed. Search indexes the extract, not the wiki.
- `README.md` may mix authored prose with one generated region. That region is a view of `@public` tethers, linted against compile. It is not a second source of doctrine.
- Rubber-stamp exists: touching tether bytes refreshes provenance. Irreducible without reading the prose. Not a judgment layer.
- Tether detects structural invalidation of attached explanations. It does not certify their truth, operator approval, or behavioral compliance. Prose and examples cannot create evidence of execution.
- Live analysis describes observed tracked working-tree inputs, not an atomic snapshot. Missing evidence is explicit coverage or an operational error, never equality. Detailed analysis contracts live in `src/facts.tether`.

# Hosts

| artifact | host |
|---|---|
| marked comment immediately preceding a declaration | that declaration (symbol) |
| `foo.ts.tether` beside `foo.ts` | file `foo.ts` |
| `src.tether` beside directory `src/` | folder `src/` |
| `root.tether` at repo root | repository |
| `AGENTS.md` / `CLAUDE.md` | honorary folder of their directory |
| tracked file inside a directory that contains `SKILL.md` | honorary (out of scope, like `SKILL.md`) |

Do not use a `.tether` file inside the folder as a second folder convention.

# Language

Closed forms. The file host is not markdown. Prose lives in `doc` bodies and may use markdown *inside* those bodies.

```
@symbol Name
@symbol Name.member
@ref path#Name
@ref #Name
@ref path
@public

doc {
  doctrine
}

example ts {
  await refreshSession(cookie)
}
```

- `@symbol Name` is a claim on the host file (inline comment or `foo.ts.tether`). The file is obvious. Gone → `symbol_missing`. Two of that name in the file → `symbol_ambiguous`. Bare `@symbol` on a folder or root tether is `ill_formed`.
- Paths are scoped to the host. You can only name what that host can see. `../` is `ill_formed`.
  - inline / `foo.ts.tether`: `@symbol Name` or `@ref #Name` (this file). `@ref sibling.ts#Other` is a child of the same directory.
  - `src.tether`: `@ref extract/types.ts#Tether` (child of `src/`).
  - `root.tether`: `@ref src/extract/types.ts#Tether` (child of the repo).
- Distant claims belong on the folder or root that can see them. Public contracts at the root use the full repo path.
- `@public` includes this tether in the public compile (folder-mirrored headings/nav, and the generated README region). Omit it: private wiki only.
- Multiple `@symbol` / `@ref` lines are a union. `@public` is a flag, not a target.
- `doc { ... }` is opaque prose. Unfenced trailing text after directives is also body.
- `example <lang> { ... }` is an opaque snippet. It is not a host, not a `@ref`, not a declaration, not a Quartz node. Extract does not parse it as code. Compile renders it as a fenced block. Use this for illustrations; do not `@ref` names that exist only inside an example.
- Fenced code inside `doc` is equally opaque. Prefer `example` so the intent is structural.
- No `@quartz` until Quartz is a released dependency.
- Inline form: a comment whose first token after the marker is `@tether`, then the same directives, `doc`, and `example` bodies.

```
/** @tether
 * @ref session.ts#Session
 * Refresh is a rename of session state, not an in-place patch.
 */
export const refreshSession = ...
```

Line comments: consecutive `// @tether` then `//` continuation lines, immediately above the declaration.

# Extract

- Adjacency: marked comment immediately preceding the declaration. Only whitespace (and language skip nodes: decorators, attributes) may sit between them. Not nearest-enclosing.
- Sidecars never auto-bind to symbols.
- Folder fingerprint = sorted tracked path + blob hash under that folder. A tracked symlink contributes the git blob of its link target. Noisy on purpose. The repository host is the folder `.`, so any commit that does not touch `root.tether` leaves it with `host_fingerprint_changed`, and correcting an inline tether flags every enclosing folder tether until it is reviewed.
- `AGENTS.md` / `CLAUDE.md` are not doctrine. They are not rogue and they are not extracted. `SKILL.md` is the same, and so is every tracked file under a directory that contains `SKILL.md`. We do not parse, compile, or babysit their bodies.
- Fingerprint = grammar-version-prefixed hash of preorder AST node types + token text, no positions, no comment extras. Rename of an emitted identifier changes it. Reformat does not.
- Shape fingerprint = fingerprint with the declaration name field replaced by `$NAME`. Used only to *list* rename candidates, never to auto-rebind.

# Facts (closed)

| kind | proven when |
|---|---|
| `rogue_document` | tracked `*.md`/`*.txt` that is an independent document: not allowlisted, not honorary, not empty or whitespace-only, and not a conventional fixture input |
| `ill_formed` | parse error, `@symbol` disagrees with adjacency, `@symbol` on a folder/root tether, or a `../` path |
| `duplicate_id` | two tethers share an explicit symbol id on the same host file |
| `host_missing` | derived host path, symbol, or directory is gone |
| `host_fingerprint_changed` | current working-tree host fingerprint ≠ fingerprint at the identified Git baseline |
| `ref_missing` | optional `@ref` target not found |
| `ref_fingerprint_changed` | that `@ref` target's fingerprint changed since the tether last changed |
| `symbol_missing` | `@symbol` on a file host names a declaration that is not in that file |
| `symbol_ambiguous` | `@symbol` matches more than one declaration in that file |
| `public_surface_stale` | the generated span in `README.md` ≠ current `@public` compile, or is absent when public tethers exist |

`ref_missing` may include `candidates` (N≤4) only when each candidate is a unique shape match in the same file or across the two git blobs. Otherwise omit the list.

`example` bodies never contribute symbols, refs, fingerprints of foreign code, or Quartz graph nodes. Changing an example only touches the tether (provenance), not a host fingerprint.

No rename kind. Missing current targets emit missing facts. Missing historical correspondence, including an inline declaration renamed while its comment stayed unchanged, is unchecked evidence; names are not silently rebound.

# Allowlist

Default allowlist is those names **at the repo root only** (`README.md`, not `docs/README.md`). Honorary / out of scope (not rogue, not extracted): `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `SKILL.md`, and every tracked file inside a directory that contains `SKILL.md`. Not documents (not rogue): empty or whitespace-only files; tracked files under `tests/fixtures`, `test/fixtures`, `scripts/fixtures`, or a `__fixtures__` directory; and `*.txt` whose name is a supported source file plus `.txt` (e.g. `service.test.ts.txt`). `.tether.json` may add extra full paths.

# CLI

JSON-first, Effect, Bun, agentic-cli family. No project-local `.tether/` cache. State under `$TETHER_HOME` or `~/.config/tether/projects/<git-key>/`. Git key = normalized origin URL, else hash of repo root.

Discover commands and executable examples through `capabilities`, `schema`, and `examples`. Workflow commands are `extract`, `lint`, `facts`, `get`, `list`, `aggregate`, `compile`, and `search`.

`lint` prints facts and evidence. Exit 1 if any fact kind is in `fail_on` (default: all kinds except fingerprint changes and duplicate IDs). That map controls policy, not coverage or truth. `changed:true` selects affected sources, including enclosing hosts and incoming references.

`get` retrieves exact tethers with live evidence. `context:true` returns applicable layers separately; it does not synthesize prose or resolve contradictory instructions. It does not use search caches.

`compile` writes two derived trees under the project cache dir, never as new repo files:

- `wiki/` — every tether, fact/coverage/comparison frontmatter, stacked bodies (symbol → file sidecar → enclosing folders → root). Symbol pages use a separate `_symbols/` namespace.
- `public/` — only `@public` tethers, same folder mirror, plus a generated nav.

`compile` also rewrites exactly one region in allowlisted `README.md`, between:

```
<!-- tether:public -->
<!-- /tether:public -->
```

Authored text outside those markers is never touched. Inside: generated headings/nav (and the public `doc` / `example` render) from the `@public` tree. If the markers are missing, compile does not edit README; lint emits `public_surface_stale` when any `@public` tether exists.

`search` is lexical + semantic over the extract (SQLite FTS5, Synthetic embeddings, fusion). It is cached exploration, not fresh evidence retrieval or session search. An ambient SYNTHETIC_API_KEY can enable networked embeddings; use lexical mode when text must stay local. Example bodies are searchable as text, not as symbols.

# Merge

Same host + bind stacks. Innermost first. Duplicate explicit ids are `duplicate_id`. Bodies are not fused into one essay.

# Languages (v1 extract)

javascript, typescript, tsx, rust, go, ruby, python via `web-tree-sitter` and grammar wasm. Language tables own comment kinds, skip kinds, declaration kinds, and name extraction. Swift is out until a loadable grammar exists.

TypeScript and TSX load a tether-owned wasm pair from `grammars/` before the npm `tree-sitter-typescript` 0.23.2 assets. Upstream still rejects an object-literal type argument on a tagged template such as sql<{ a: string }>`SELECT 1` (issues #341/#329) and treats `import("m").T` as a non-primary type, so `[]`, `<...>`, `["k"]`, and `readonly` fail (issues #322/#352). The vendored files are tag v0.23.2 plus `grammars/tree-sitter-typescript.diff`: PR #332 (`instantiation_expression` as the `template_call` function), import() types as a composable `primary_type` with optional type arguments, PR #358 (`export type *` / `export type * as ns`, issue #348), and a literal `&` in JSX text (tree-sitter-javascript issue #366; HTML entities are optional in JSX). `typeof import("m")` as a call type argument is recovered in extract when the only ERROR/MISSING nodes span that form.

Rust loads a tether-owned wasm from `grammars/` before the npm `tree-sitter-rust` 0.24.0 asset. Upstream 0.24.0 reads `&raw` as the start of `&raw const|mut` and emits ERROR when `raw` is an ordinary identifier. The vendored file is tag v0.24.0 plus `grammars/tree-sitter-rust.diff` (PR #288: `raw` is a reserved identifier so `&raw` falls back to a normal borrow). Rebuild with `bun run rebuild:grammars` (`tree-sitter build --wasm --docker`, emscripten/emsdk:3.1.64, sha256 in `grammars/manifest.json`). Drop each override when an upstream release parses those forms.

Product: every named declaration the grammar can see (functions, types, methods, fields, …) is a possible host. One parse per file. Incremental on dirty files is enough for normal repos. The limiter is not node count — it is ambiguous names in the same file (`symbol_ambiguous`). A tether never searches the whole repo for a name.

Elixir and C++ are out of this cut.

# Out of v1

Quartz-powered refs. Session search. A second attest command. Mild warnings. Bind tables. A committed `docs/` wiki. Examples participating in the symbol graph.

# Runtime

Git subprocesses use one `node:child_process` helper in `src/core/git.ts#runGit`.
Walk and lint call that helper. `trimStdout` defaults on for core identity commands
and off for blob/NUL output (`git show`, `ls-files -z`, blame, diffs). ENOENT maps
to `GitNotFoundError`. Effect interruption kills the child.

Compiled packages exist-check WASM beside the executable before `Parser.init`, so
missing assets yield a doctor envelope instead of empty stdout.

# Release

npm `@skastr0/tether` and `@skastr0/tether-{darwin,linux}-{arm64,x64}` publish from
`.github/workflows/npm-publish.yml` on a `v*` tag, through npm Trusted Publishing
(OIDC) and the GitHub `release` environment, which requires `skastr0` approval.
No local npm credential is needed. `npm trust list <package> --json` inspects the
trusted publisher.

CI (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`) runs verify, pack, and native smoke on macos-15,
macos-15-intel, ubuntu-24.04, and ubuntu-24.04-arm, with no Bun on PATH. Tag only
after CI is green on the commit.

Published: 0.1.0 (bootstrap `Bun.spawn` build, superseded), 0.2.0, 0.2.1, 0.2.2, 0.2.3. `v0.1.1`
was tagged and never published. Never republish a version. A partial upload requires
inspecting exact registry versions and integrity before resuming; differing bytes
require a new version. Windows and Linux musl are unsupported.

}
